course: dictionary
lesson: 13703
title: Insider
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An insider is someone who belongs to a group, club, company or organisation, so they know how it works and what is happening inside it. «Mia knew the secret password because she is an insider at the club.» Mia is part of the club, so she knows things that people outside the club do not.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like «secret», «knew» and «belongs» tell you that an insider has special knowledge. Try the swap check: «Mia knew the secret password because she is a member of the club» still makes sense, so insider means someone who is part of the group.
explain: Insider information is secret knowledge that only people inside a group have. «The thief was an insider who worked at the bank, so he knew where the money was kept.» The insider is the person, and the secret knowledge is the insider information.
fact: An insider is a person who belongs to a group, club, company or organisation.
fact: An insider knows how the group works and what is happening inside it.
fact: «Insider information» means secret knowledge that only people inside a group have.
fact: In detective stories, «an insider» can be someone who helped the thief from inside the place they stole from.
fact: Insider trading means using secret company information to buy or sell shares, and it is a crime.
exercise: «The thief was an insider who worked at the bank.» What is an insider? | A person who works in a shop across the road | A bank robber wearing a mask | *A person who belongs to a group and knows what is happening inside it | A person who is always late
exercise: Lena has «insider tips» about the new game because her older brother works at the company. What are insider tips? | *Secret advice from someone who knows how the company works | Tips printed in the newspaper for everyone | Tips about cooking pasta | Tips from a stranger in the street
exercise: Which word means a person who belongs to a group and knows its secrets? | river | *insider | sunshine | club
test: «Insider information» means what? | Information written in a foreign language | Facts that everyone already knows from the newspaper | Information shouted from the top of a hill | *Secret knowledge that only people inside a group have
test: Why is insider trading a crime? | *It uses secret company information to buy or sell shares | It involves too many people in one room | It is a kind of sport played in teams | It makes people laugh at parties
exam: Which sentence uses insider correctly? | *After two years at the company, Raj was an insider who knew all its plans. | Mum said the insider was a big red bus. | The sign on the shop door said «insider» in big red letters. | The insider ate a sandwich on the bus to school.
